<li>The 2 triangles are oriented such that upper A corresponds to upper X, upper B corresponds to upper Y, and upper C corresponds to upper Z.</li>
<li>Triangle upper A upper B upper C is labeled as follows:<br>
<ul>
<li>The measure of angle upper A is 60°.</li>
<li>The length of side upper A upper C is d.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>A note indicates the figures are not drawn to scale.</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">For the triangles shown, triangle <math alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mrow>
	<mi>A</mi>
	<mi>B</mi>
	<mi>C</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is dilated by a scale factor of <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> to obtain triangle <math alttext="upper X upper Y upper Z"><mrow>
	<mi>X</mi>
	<mi>Y</mi>
	<mi>Z</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, where <math alttext="d equals 16"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext="upper X"><mi>X</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b9582861-b56a-4bdf-9ad9-b881b136641d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7f694a1d-03dd-48a9-8469-98df45c29eb6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"57\"><mn>57</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4528145c-ebe7-4e68-a383-0fb0755eb57c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d74b72fc-44ae-40b4-a880-34fa1feeeeba","content":"<p><math alttext=\"63\"><mn>63</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4528145c-ebe7-4e68-a383-0fb0755eb57c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. It's given that triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper X upper Y upper Z"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></math> is obtained by a dilation of triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. It follows that triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A upper B upper C"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper X upper Y upper Z"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math> corresponds to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper X"><mi>X</mi></math>. Since corresponding angles in similar triangles have the same measure and the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="60"><mn>60</mn></math> degrees, it follows that the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper X"><mi>X</mi></math> is also <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="60"><mn>60</mn></math> degrees.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors. &nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e0d2e21a","external_id":"c6d50efa-46fb-4406-9c84-8c8d2ab9e927","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"dcef6a0d-5a14-46c2-b671-7d542bcbda49","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"367.985\" height=\"200.527\" viewBox=\"0 0 367.985 200.527\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Triangle upper A upper B upper C and triangle upper X upper Y upper Z. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"bdb5c0b7-bc52-4257-a8b5-8d670c59b969\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><polygon points=\"62.052 111.17 17.666 34.292 106.438 34.292 62.052 111.17\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><polygon points=\"276.262 136.317 202.191 8.021 350.334 8.021 276.262 136.317\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><path d=\"M8.411,33.217v-.048c0-.006-.01-.02-.029-.039a.157.157,0,0,0-.077-.039c-.033-.006-.078-.012-.136-.019s-.136-.013-.233-.019-.213-.013-.349-.02-.3-.01-.484-.01H6.454q-.408,0-1.8.1a3.6,3.6,0,0,0-.523.775q-.465.775-.911,1.686a3.758,3.758,0,0,0-.446,1.2.439.439,0,0,0,.272.368,1.543,1.543,0,0,0,.494.194,2.179,2.179,0,0,0,.3.039c.026,0,.039.039.039.116a.89.89,0,0,1-.1.407q-1.8-.1-1.841-.1-.369,0-.649.019c-.187.013-.391.025-.61.039s-.433.025-.64.038A.223.223,0,0,1,0,37.752c0-.245.045-.368.136-.368a2.182,2.182,0,0,0,.591-.116,1.177,1.177,0,0,0,.533-.291,10.8,10.8,0,0,0,1.182-1.822l5.349-9.612a.859.859,0,0,1,.756-.523.345.345,0,0,1,.155.039L10.31,35.291q.193,1.221.233,1.4c.039.193.2.358.494.494a1.778,1.778,0,0,0