e measure of angle upper A is 60°.</li>\n<li>The length of side upper A upper C is d.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figures are not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For the triangles shown, triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is dilated by a scale factor of <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> to obtain triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, where <math alttext=\"d equals 16\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>. What is the measure, in degrees, of angle <math alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b9582861-b56a-4bdf-9ad9-b881b136641d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7f694a1d-03dd-48a9-8469-98df45c29eb6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"57\"><mn>57</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4528145c-ebe7-4e68-a383-0fb0755eb57c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d74b72fc-44ae-40b4-a880-34fa1feeeeba","content":"<p><math alttext=\"63\"><mn>63</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["4528145c-ebe7-4e68-a383-0fb0755eb57c"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. It's given that triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></math> is obtained by a dilation of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. It follows that triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is similar to triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi><mi>Z</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> corresponds to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi></math>. Since corresponding angles in similar triangles have the same measure and the measure of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn></math> degrees, it follows that the measure of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi></math> is also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"60\"><mn>60</mn></math> degrees.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors. &nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017723,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"e0d2e21a","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1755117017723,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"c6d50efa-46fb-4406-9c84-8c8d2ab9e927","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"dcef6a0d-5a14-46c2-b671-7d542bcbda49","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"367.985\" height=\"200.527\" viewBox=\"0 0 367.985 200.527\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Triangle upper A upper B upper C and triangle upper X upper Y upper Z. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"bdb5c0b7-bc52-4257-a8b5-8d670c59b969\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><polygon points=\"62.052 111.17 17.666 34.292 106.438 34.292 62.052 111.17\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><polygon points=\"276.262 136.317 202.191 8.02