	<mn>2,880</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>36</mn>
		<mi>h</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="36"><mn>36</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="80 equals h"><mrow>
	<mn>80</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>h</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the height, in units, of the prism is <math alttext="80"><mn>80</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the height, in units, of a right square prism where the length of the edge of the base is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> units and the volume of the prism is <math alttext="144 StartRoot 30 EndRoot"><mn>144</mn><msqrt><mn>30</mn></msqrt></math>, not <math alttext="2,880"><mn>2,880</mn>
</math>, units.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the area, in square units, of the base, not the height, in units, of the prism.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the height, in units, of a right square prism where the length of the edge of the base is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
