</math>, units.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e4b4e9ea","external_id":"9d90d9a2-0084-4cae-be11-73b040f11c9e","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"32e171b5-f00e-4f92-a347-23f8e7987dd3","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>The length of the edge of the base of a right square prism is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> units. The volume of the prism is <math alttext=\"2,880\"><mn>2,880</mn>\n</math> cubic units. What is the height, in units, of the prism?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4656d200-10f8-411c-a395-478ee9174ebd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4 StartRoot 30 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>30</mn>\n\t</msqrt>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"97213f23-c8f8-40cd-844e-34c72d25e4ef","content":"<p><math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8224daa3-3bb9-452f-9e15-eafd5679ef60","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24 StartRoot 5 EndRoot\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n\t<msqrt>\n\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t</msqrt>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"88f8d506-6f17-43c4-9155-8b5bf06b2dd9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["88f8d506-6f17-43c4-9155-8b5bf06b2dd9"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. The volume, <math alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi>\n</math>, of a right square prism is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper V equals s squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi>\n</math> represents the length of the edge of the base and <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> represents the height of the prism. It&rsquo;s given that the volume of a right square prism is <math alttext=\"2,880\"><mn>2,880</mn>\n</mat