right parenthesis squared right parenthesis plus y squared equals 0 plus left parenthesis StartFraction 58 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>58</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>58</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x squared plus 58 x plus 841 right parenthesis plus y squared equals 841\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>841</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>841</mn></math>. This equation is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 29 right parenthesis squared plus y squared equals 841\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>841</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus left parenthesis negative 29 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 0 right parenthesis squared equals 841\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>841</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 29\"><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math>, and the coordinates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of the center of the circle are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 29 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017719,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"ee540927","skill_cd":"S.D.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Circles","createDate":1755117017719,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"6899531e-bbaf-4fee-900a-53c4fc396050","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"881e383c-096e-454d-8a30-cac174e0d6da","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x squared plus 58 x plus y squared equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>58</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the <em>xy</em>-plane, the graph of the given equation is a circle. What are the coordinates <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><