th xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>. By completing the square, the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared plus 58 x plus y squared equals 0\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x squared plus 58 x plus left parenthesis StartFraction 58 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared right parenthesis plus y squared equals 0 plus left parenthesis StartFraction 58 Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>58</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>58</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x squared plus 58 x plus 841 right parenthesis plus y squared equals 841\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>841</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>841</mn></math>. This equation is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 29 right parenthesis squared plus y squared equals 841\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>841</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus left parenthesis negative 29 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 0 right parenthesis squared equals 841\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>841</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 29\"><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn></math>, and the coordinates <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of the center of the circle are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 29 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"6899531e-bbaf-4fee-900a-53c4fc396050","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017719,"updateDate":1755117017719}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017719, 1755117017719),
    ($SATQ$eeb4143c$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$070631-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Lines, angles, and triangles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference ">
