$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The area of triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span> above is at least 48 but <span class="formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both "></span>no more than 60. If <span class="italic">y</span> is an integer, what is one <span class="formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both "></span>possible value of <span class="italic">x</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["either","or"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is either <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_001_d014579d.png" alt="the fraction 10 over 3"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_002_1ee4a014.png" alt="the fraction 15 over 4"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_003_5a5113a2.png" alt="the fraction 25 over 6"></span>. The area of triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span> can be expressed as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_004_8ce3d221.png" alt="one half times, open parenthesis, 5 plus 7, close parenthesis, times y"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_005_b453fd92.png" alt="6 y"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that the area of triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span> is at least 48 but no more than 60. It follows that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_006_e3fd0441.png" alt="48 is less than or equal to 6 y, which is less than or equal to 60"></span>. Dividing by 6 to isolate <span class="italic">y</span> in this compound inequality yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_007_70a7c86e.png" alt="8 is less than or equal to y, which is less than or equal to 10"></span>. Since <span class="italic">y</span> is an integer, <span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_008_2d3795f3.png" alt="y equals 8, 9, or 10"></span></span>. In the given figure, the two right triangles shown are similar because they have two pairs of congruent angles: their respective right angles and angle <span class="italic">A</span>. Therefore, the following proportion is true: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_009_e851481d.png" alt="the fraction x over y equals the fraction 5 over 12"></span>. Substituting 8 for <span class="italic">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_010_7b31adf2.png" alt="the fraction x over 8 equals the fraction 5 over 12"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class="italic">x</span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_011_d014579d.png" alt="the fraction 10 over 3"></span>. Substituting 9 for <span class="italic">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_012_13905ab8.png" alt="the fraction x over 9 equals the fraction 5 over 12"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class="italic">x</span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_013_1ee4a014.png" alt="the fraction 15 over 4"></span>. Substituting 10 for <span class="italic">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_014_672fbcee.png" alt="the fraction x over 10 equals the fraction 5 over 12"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class="italic">x</span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_015_5a5113a2.png" alt="the fraction 25 over 6"></span>. Note that 10/3, 15/4, 25/6, 3.333, 3.75, 4.166, and 4.167 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
$SATQ$, true, 16, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$SPR$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"eeb4143c","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"070631-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"spr","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_000_7ee578ad.png\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle A B C, where angle C is a right angle. Side A C is horizontal, such that vertex A is to the left of vertex C, and vertex B is directly above vertex C. A vertical line segment is drawn from a point on side A B to a point on side A C and divides side A C into two segments. The length of the segment between vertex A and the vertical line segment is labeled 5 and the length of the segment between the vertical line segment and vertex C is labeled 7. The vertical line segment is labeled x. Side B C is labeled y. A note states the figure is not drawn to scale.\" width=\"133\" height=\"100\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The area of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> above is at least 48 but <span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span>no more than 60. If <span class=\"italic\">y</span> is an integer, what is one <span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span>possible value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answerOptions":null,"keys":null,"correct_answer":["either","or"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is either <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_001_d014579d.png\" alt=\"the fraction 10 over 3\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_002_1ee4a014.png\" alt=\"the fraction 15 over 4\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_003_5a5113a2.png\" alt=\"the fraction 25 over 6\"></span>. The area of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> can be expressed as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_004_8ce3d221.png\" alt=\"one half times, open parenthesis, 5 plus 7, close parenthesis, times y\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_005_b453fd92.png\" alt=\"6 y\"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that the area of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> is at least 48 but no more than 60. It follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_006_e3fd0441.png\" alt=\"48 is less than or equal to 6 y, which is less than or equal to 60\"></span>. Dividing by 6 to isolate <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in this compound inequality yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_007_70a7c86e.png\" alt=\"8 is less than or equal to y, which is less than or equal to 10\"></span>. Since <span class=\"italic\">y</span> is an integer, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_008_2d3795f3.png\" alt=\"y equals 8, 9, or 10\"></span></span>. In the given figure, the two right triangles shown are similar because they have two pairs of congruent angles: their respective right angles and angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span>. Therefore, the following proportion is true: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_009_e851481d.png\" alt=\"the fraction x over y equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Substituting 8 for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_010_7b31adf2.png\" alt=\"the fraction x over 8 equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_011_d014579d.png\" alt=\"the fraction 10 over 3\"></span>. Substituting 9 for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_012_13905ab8.png\" alt=\"the fraction x over 9 equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_013_1ee4a014.png\" alt=\"the fraction 15 over 4\"></span>. Substituting 10 for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_014_672fbcee.png\" alt=\"the fraction x over 10 equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/eeb4143c/img_015_5a5113a2.png\" alt=\"the fraction 25 over 6\"></span>. Note that 10/3, 15/4, 25/6, 3.333, 3.75, 4.166, and 4.167 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":16,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959632,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"eeb4143c","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959632,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"070631-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"84122363-e5b6-464c-a789-05363f3f1e60","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"070631-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle A B C, where angle C is a right angle. Side A C is horizontal, such that vertex A is to the left of vertex C, and vertex B is directly above vertex C. A vertical line segment is drawn from a point on side A B to a point on side A C and divides side A C into two segments. The length of the segment between vertex A and the vertical line segment is labeled 5 and the length of the segment between the vertical line segment and vertex C is labeled 7. The vertical line segment is labeled x. Side B C is labeled y. A note states the figure is not drawn to scale.\" width=\"133\" height=\"100\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The area of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> above is at least 48 but <span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span>no more than 60. If <span class=\"italic\">y</span> is an integer, what is one <span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span>possible value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is either <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 10 over 3\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 15 over 4\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 25 over 6\"></span>. The area of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> can be expressed as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"one half times, open parenthesis, 5 plus 7, close parenthesis, times y\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"6 y\"></span>. It&rsquo;s given that the area of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ABC</span> is at least 48 but no more than 60. It follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"48 is less than or equal to 6 y, which is less than or equal to 60\"></span>. Dividing by 6 to isolate <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in this compound inequality yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"8 is less than or equal to y, which is less than or equal to 10\"></span>. Since <span class=\"italic\">y</span> is an integer, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals 8, 9, or 10\"></span></span>. In the given figure, the two right triangles shown are similar because they have two pairs of congruent angles: their respective right angles and angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span>. Therefore, the following proportion is true: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction x over y equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Substituting 8 for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction x over 8 equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 10 over 3\"></span>. Substituting 9 for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction x over 9 equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 15 over 4\"></span>. Substituting 10 for <span class=\"italic\">y</span> in the proportion results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction x over 10 equals the fraction 5 over 12\"></span>. Cross multiplying and solving for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 25 over 6\"></span>. Note that 10/3, 15/4, 25/6, 3.333, 3.75, 4.166, and 4.167 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959632,"updateDate":1691007959632,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959632, 1691007959632),
