<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from subtracting the measure of angle <math alttext="upper C"><mi>C</mi>
</math> from the measure of angle <math alttext="upper B"><mi>B</mi>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from adding the measures of angles <math alttext="upper B"><mi>B</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="upper C"><mi>C</mi>
</math> but not subtracting the result from <math alttext="180 degree"><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"f1747a6a","external_id":"6145108f-5273-4b08-afde-8e75072e2eef","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"48610901-a4d9-423f-8379-99b8ecb45085","uId":"94ed12e3-a176-401a-8cf0-3a581702d099","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi>B</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"52 degree\"><mrow><mn>52</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"17 degree\"><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"94365c19-5289-443f-a559-1b995d2ba3c2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"21 degree\"><mn>21</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"d4311f94-a586-4349-8101-727e3658d1cd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"35 degree\"><mn>35</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"e0f787e1-4273-41c4-8e39-52c7739711bf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"69 degree\"><mn>69</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"6d7649ca-5880-427f-abba-fa5545e70408","content":"<p><math alttext=\"111 degree\"><mn>111</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}],"keys":["6d7649ca-5880-427f-abba-fa5545e70408"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. The sum of the angle measures of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Adding the measures of angles <math alttext=\"upper B\"><mi